            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tension-type headache (TTH) is the most common form of headache in the community, affecting up to 80% of people from time to time. At least 10% of people experience episodic TTH on a frequent basis (up to 14 days per month) and the condition is chronic for 2- 3%.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
